{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"Adult primary liver cancer is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the tissues of the liver.","source_span":"Adult primary liver cancer is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the tissues of the liver."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"The two types of adult primary liver cancer are hepatocellular carcinoma and cholangiocarcinoma (bile duct cancer).","source_span":"The two types of adult primary liver cancer are: - Hepatocellular carcinoma. - Cholangiocarcinoma (bile duct cancer)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"Hepatocellular carcinoma, the most common type of adult primary liver cancer, is the third leading cause of cancer-related deaths worldwide.","source_span":"The most common type of adult primary liver cancer is hepatocellular carcinoma. This type of liver cancer is the third leading cause of cancer-related deaths worldwide."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"The liver has four lobes and fills the upper right side of the abdomen inside the rib cage.","source_span":"It has four lobes and fills the upper right side of the abdomen inside the rib cage."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"Having both hepatitis B and hepatitis C increases the risk of adult primary liver cancer even more than having just one.","source_span":"Having both hepatitis B and hepatitis C increases the risk even more."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"Hemochromatosis causes the body to store more iron than it needs, with extra iron stored in the liver, heart, and pancreas.","source_span":"Having hemochromatosis, a condition in which the body takes up and stores more iron than it needs. The extra iron is stored in the liver, heart, and pancreas"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"Eating foods tainted with aflatoxin, a poison from a fungus that grows on improperly stored grains and nuts, is a risk factor for adult primary liver cancer.","source_span":"Eating foods tainted with aflatoxin (poison from a fungus that can grow on foods, such as grains and nuts, that have not been stored properly)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"An increased level of alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) in the blood may indicate liver cancer, but AFP is sometimes normal even when liver cancer is present.","source_span":"An increased level of alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) in the blood may be a sign of liver cancer...Sometimes the AFP level is normal even when there is liver cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","statement":"Triple-phase CT takes images at three different times after dye injection to get the best picture of abnormal areas in the liver.","source_span":"Images may be taken at three different times after the dye is injected, to get the best picture of abnormal areas in the liver. This is called triple-phase CT."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What are the two types of adult primary liver cancer?","answer":"Hepatocellular carcinoma and cholangiocarcinoma (bile duct cancer)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Which type of adult primary liver cancer is most common, and where does it rank among causes of cancer death worldwide?","answer":"Hepatocellular carcinoma is the most common type of adult primary liver cancer and is the third leading cause of cancer-related deaths worldwide."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","fact_refs":[3],"question":"How many lobes does the liver have and where is it located?","answer":"The liver has four lobes and fills the upper right side of the abdomen inside the rib cage."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Does having both hepatitis B and hepatitis C affect liver cancer risk differently than having just one?","answer":"Yes, having both hepatitis B and hepatitis C increases the risk of adult primary liver cancer even more than having just one."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What is hemochromatosis and where does the excess iron get stored in the body?","answer":"Hemochromatosis is a condition in which the body takes up and stores more iron than it needs; the extra iron is stored in the liver, heart, and pancreas."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_1","fact_refs":[7],"question":"Is an elevated AFP level always present when someone has liver cancer?","answer":"No, an increased AFP level may signal liver cancer, but sometimes the AFP level is normal even when liver cancer is present."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"Bile duct cancer is a rare disease in which malignant cells form in the bile ducts and is also called cholangiocarcinoma.","source_span":"Bile duct cancer is a rare disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the bile ducts...Bile duct cancer is also called cholangiocarcinoma."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"There are two types of bile duct cancer: intrahepatic bile duct cancer and extrahepatic bile duct cancer.","source_span":"There are two types of bile duct cancer: - Intrahepatic bile duct cancer...- Extrahepatic bile duct cancer"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"Perihilar bile duct cancer, found in the hilum region, is also called a Klatskin tumor or perihilar cholangiocarcinoma.","source_span":"Perihilar bile duct cancer is also called a Klatskin tumor or perihilar cholangiocarcinoma."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"The distal region is made up of the common bile duct, which passes through the pancreas and ends in the small intestine.","source_span":"The distal region is made up of the common bile duct which passes through the pancreas and ends in the small intestine."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"Risk factors for bile duct cancer include primary sclerosing cholangitis, chronic ulcerative colitis, cysts in the bile ducts, and infection with a Chinese liver fluke parasite.","source_span":"Risk factors for bile duct cancer include the following conditions: - Primary sclerosing cholangitis...- Chronic ulcerative colitis. - Cysts in the bile ducts...- Infection with a Chinese liver fluke parasite."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"Signs of bile duct cancer include jaundice, abdominal pain, dark urine, clay colored stool, fever, itchy skin, nausea and vomiting, and unexplained weight loss.","source_span":"Signs of bile duct cancer include jaundice and pain in the abdomen...Dark urine. Clay colored stool...Itchy skin."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"Higher than normal levels of carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) and CA 19-9 tumor markers may indicate bile duct cancer.","source_span":"Higher than normal levels of carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) and CA 19-9 may mean there is bile duct cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","statement":"Liver function tests for bile duct cancer measure the amounts of bilirubin and alkaline phosphatase released into the blood by the liver.","source_span":"A procedure in which a blood sample is checked to measure the amounts of bilirubin and alkaline phosphatase released into the blood by the liver."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What is another name for bile duct cancer?","answer":"Bile duct cancer is also called cholangiocarcinoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What are the two main types of bile duct cancer?","answer":"Intrahepatic bile duct cancer and extrahepatic bile duct cancer."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What is perihilar bile duct cancer also known as?","answer":"It is also called a Klatskin tumor or perihilar cholangiocarcinoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What organ does the common bile duct pass through in the distal region before ending in the small intestine?","answer":"The pancreas."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What conditions are known risk factors for bile duct cancer?","answer":"Primary sclerosing cholangitis, chronic ulcerative colitis, cysts in the bile ducts, and infection with a Chinese liver fluke parasite."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_2","fact_refs":[6],"question":"Which two tumor markers, when elevated, may indicate bile duct cancer?","answer":"Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) and CA 19-9."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Childhood liver cancer is a disease in which malignant cells form in the tissues of the liver, and it is rare in children and adolescents.","source_span":"Childhood liver cancer is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the tissues of the liver...Liver cancer is rare in children and adolescents."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Hepatoblastoma is the most common type of childhood liver cancer and usually affects children younger than 3 years of age.","source_span":"Hepatoblastoma is the most common type of childhood liver cancer. It usually affects children younger than 3 years of age."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Hepatocellular carcinoma in children usually affects older children and adolescents and is more common in areas of Asia with high rates of hepatitis infection than in the U.S.","source_span":"Hepatocellular carcinoma usually affects older children and adolescents. It is more common in areas of Asia that have high rates of hepatitis infection than in the U.S."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Undifferentiated embryonal sarcoma of the liver usually occurs in children between 5 and 10 years of age and often spreads throughout the liver and/or to the lungs.","source_span":"Undifferentiated embryonal sarcoma of the liver: This type of liver cancer usually occurs in children between 5 and 10 years of age. It often spreads all through the liver and/or to the lungs."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Infantile choriocarcinoma of the liver is a very rare tumor that starts in the placenta and spreads to the fetus, usually found during the first few months of life.","source_span":"Infantile choriocarcinoma of the liver is a very rare tumor that starts in the placenta and spreads to the fetus. The tumor is usually found during the first few months of life."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Risk factors for hepatoblastoma include Aicardi syndrome, Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome, familial adenomatous polyposis, glycogen storage disease, very low birth weight, Simpson-Golabi-Behmel syndrome, and Trisomy 18.","source_span":"Risk factors for hepatoblastoma include the following syndromes or conditions: - Aicardi syndrome. - Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome. - Familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP). - Glycogen storage disease. - A very low weight at birth. - Simpson-Golabi-Behmel syndrome. - Certain genetic changes, such as Trisomy 18."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in children include Alagille syndrome, glycogen storage disease, hepatitis B virus infection passed from mother to child at birth, progressive familial intrahepatic disease, and tyrosinemia.","source_span":"Risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma include the following syndromes or conditions: - Alagille syndrome. - Glycogen storage disease. - Hepatitis B virus infection that was passed from mother to child at birth. - Progressive familial intrahepatic disease. - Tyrosinemia."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"Some patients with tyrosinemia or progressive familial intrahepatic disease will have a liver transplant before there are signs or symptoms of cancer.","source_span":"Some patients with tyrosinemia or progressive familial intrahepatic disease will have a liver transplant before there are signs or symptoms of cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","statement":"The blood of children with liver cancer may have increased amounts of beta-human chorionic gonadotropin (β-hCG) or alpha-fetoprotein (AFP).","source_span":"The blood of children who have liver cancer may have increased amounts of a hormone called beta-human chorionic gonadotropin (-hCG) or a protein called alpha-fetoprotein (AFP)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What is the most common type of childhood liver cancer, and what age group does it usually affect?","answer":"Hepatoblastoma is the most common type of childhood liver cancer; it usually affects children younger than 3 years of age."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Which type of childhood liver cancer usually affects older children and adolescents and is more common in parts of Asia with high hepatitis rates?","answer":"Hepatocellular carcinoma usually affects older children and adolescents and is more common in areas of Asia with high rates of hepatitis infection than in the U.S."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","fact_refs":[3],"question":"At what age does undifferentiated embryonal sarcoma of the liver typically occur, and where does it often spread?","answer":"It usually occurs in children between 5 and 10 years of age and often spreads throughout the liver and/or to the lungs."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What is unusual about infantile choriocarcinoma of the liver and when is it usually discovered?","answer":"It is a very rare tumor that starts in the placenta and spreads to the fetus, and it is usually found during the first few months of life."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What syndromes or conditions are risk factors for hepatoblastoma?","answer":"Risk factors include Aicardi syndrome, Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome, familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), glycogen storage disease, very low birth weight, Simpson-Golabi-Behmel syndrome, and genetic changes such as Trisomy 18."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000007_3","fact_refs":[8],"question":"What two substances may be found at increased levels in the blood of children with liver cancer?","answer":"Beta-human chorionic gonadotropin (β-hCG) and alpha-fetoprotein (AFP)."}
